1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,500
(Previously)
Suzuki, are you still reading BL?

2
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:08,433
Can you stop picking on our Suzuki?

3
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:09,700
I like BL too.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:10,967
We've read it too.

5
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:15,033
It feels like such a gentle world.

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,233
I'm really happy right now.

7
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,533
So cute...

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,400
After I became friends with
The Popular Clique's Big Four...

9
00:00:29,933 --> 00:00:31,543
- It's fried chicken!
- Fried chicken is here.

10
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:33,767
Isn't it the same as always?

11
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,100
It's even homemade.

12
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,409
You really want some, don't you?

13
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:37,433
Shut up.

14
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:40,367
Let me see...

15
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:44,800
So that weird setup
was to get Suzuki to write a novel.

16
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:45,800
Makes sense.
Yeah.

17
00:00:46,567 --> 00:00:48,900
I thought it was just
Serizawa being weird again.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,800
But honestly, he's still
just messing around.

19
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:52,133
True that.

20
00:00:52,233 --> 00:00:56,100
Now I can talk about
BL in front of everyone.

21
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,933
So, did you actually write anything?

22
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:00,267
Yeah.

23
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,367
Yeah, but I've only just started.

24
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:05,700
Color me intrigued.

25
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,833
Let me see.

26
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:08,276
I want to read Suzuki's novel too.

27
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:09,900
Iwasaki, don't you only read manga?

28
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,567
If Suzuki wrote it, I'd read it.

29
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:12,733
Seriously?

30
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:18,600
Feeding Suzuki like this
reminds me of that time.

31
00:01:19,467 --> 00:01:20,967
You know, Usami.

32
00:01:21,967 --> 00:01:23,133
Usami?

33
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:24,767
Teacher Usami?

34
00:01:24,867 --> 00:01:26,633
Alright, here we go!

35
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:28,167
Okay, let's warm up first.

36
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:29,133
Not that.

37
00:01:29,233 --> 00:01:32,100
Remember when we went to the
ranch for our freshman field trip?

38
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,067
I mean the rabbit from back then.

39
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:35,300
A rabbit?

40
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,433
Yeah.

41
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:39,133
Serizawa kept screaming,
'So cute, so cute!'

42
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:41,133
And he kept feeding it.

43
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,533
It ended up eating so
much it couldn't even move.

44
00:01:43,633 --> 00:01:47,000
- Right! I felt so bad for it.
- Tell me about it.

45
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,633
- It just ate way too much.
- That rabbit was super cute, though.

46
00:01:51,433 --> 00:01:53,167
I really wanted to take it home with me.

47
00:01:54,067 --> 00:01:55,867
Suzuki, you'd better watch out.

48
00:01:55,967 --> 00:01:58,700
Serizawa might not look it,
but he's actually pretty possessive.

49
00:01:58,900 --> 00:01:59,800
Huh?
What?

50
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:01,967
No, I'm not.

51
00:02:02,067 --> 00:02:03,900
I'm a devoted seme.

52
00:02:04,467 --> 00:02:05,633
Right, Suzuki?

53
00:02:06,467 --> 00:02:07,833
How is that devoted?

54
00:02:08,133 --> 00:02:09,433
You're just being selfish.

55
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:10,033
Exactly.

56
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:11,300
See?

57
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,240
That's not devoted at all.

58
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,233
But...

59
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:32,900
Sorry.

60
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:34,593
You had some ketchup on your face.

61
00:02:35,633 --> 00:02:37,867
Oh, thanks.

62
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:42,433
Sometimes, I really don't get it.

63
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,467
By the way.

64
00:02:48,567 --> 00:02:50,267
Suzuki, you're way too skinny.

65
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:52,067
Are you eating properly?

66
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:53,533
Yeah.
Yeah.

67
00:02:54,367 --> 00:02:55,867
Hey, stop touching him.

68
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:02,400
Eat more and grow up fast.

69
00:03:04,033 --> 00:03:05,733
What are you, his mom?

70
00:03:06,333 --> 00:03:09,733
Is this... what having friends feels like?

71
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:11,067
Mom?

72
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:13,633
Is Serizawa your mom?

73
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:15,200
Mommy~

74
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:57,733
Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me

75
00:03:59,733 --> 00:04:01,800
(Episode 4)
Seriously? Then hand me that.

76
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:03,067
No, I'm serious.

77
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:06,533
Uh, who's absent today?

78
00:04:06,633 --> 00:04:08,067
Oh, just Serizawa.

79
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,467
- That's rare.
- What happened to Serizawa?

80
00:04:10,567 --> 00:04:11,567
He has a fever.

81
00:04:11,633 --> 00:04:12,400
Is he okay?
Yeah.

82
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:15,767
I think he went to the
clinic to get some meds.

83
00:04:15,867 --> 00:04:17,300
He should be fine.

84
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:19,720
Plus, my notifications have
been blowing up since earlier.

85
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:27,167
(Besties Group Chat) "Hey~ → Dog → Coloring
book → Picture diary → Ticket → Pudding"

86
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:28,967
What is he doing?

87
00:04:29,067 --> 00:04:30,100
What does this mean?

88
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,200
Huh?

89
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:33,867
Oh, that's it.

90
00:04:33,967 --> 00:04:35,276
He's playing word chain by himself.

91
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:36,800
The one we always play.

92
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,500
Playing word chain all alone.

93
00:04:38,606 --> 00:04:40,995
(*In Japanese word chain, words
ending in 'n' lose) - And he even lost.

94
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:43,433
But it feels like something's missing.

95
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,500
It's so quiet without Serizawa here.

96
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:49,120
(Besties Group Chat) "Hey~ → Dog → Coloring
book → Picture diary → Ticket → Pudding"

97
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,833
Ah, Serizawa is on duty today.

98
00:04:56,933 --> 00:04:58,833
I actually had a favor to ask him.

99
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:00,500
I'll do it.

100
00:05:01,067 --> 00:05:04,867
Oh~ That's Takeuchi for you, so thoughtful.

101
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,400
Thanks.

102
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,500
Alright.

103
00:05:27,367 --> 00:05:28,700
Takeuchi.

104
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:30,967
Oh, Suzuki.

105
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:32,067
Let me help you.

106
00:05:32,167 --> 00:05:34,733
Really? Then could you get the top part?

107
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:36,067
Thanks.

108
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:40,167
By the way, has Serizawa sent any messages?

109
00:05:40,267 --> 00:05:43,000
Nope, I've already called him three times.

110
00:05:48,467 --> 00:05:52,067
"Serizawa, are you okay? Do you need
anything? Want me to bring you something?"

111
00:05:57,667 --> 00:05:58,867
What's wrong?

112
00:06:01,367 --> 00:06:06,700
Well... I'm a little worried about
Serizawa. I wonder how he's doing.

113
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:09,467
He sent a bunch of messages this morning.

114
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:11,527
But he suddenly went
radio silent this afternoon.

115
00:06:16,267 --> 00:06:18,700
You don't think he passed out, do you?

116
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:24,867
Hey, Suzuki.

117
00:06:25,333 --> 00:06:26,467
Yeah?

118
00:06:27,267 --> 00:06:31,200
I don't know if I should ask this, but...

119
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,033
Suzuki...

120
00:06:38,733 --> 00:06:40,533
Do you like Serizawa?

121
00:06:41,433 --> 00:06:42,767
Huh?

122
00:06:44,133 --> 00:06:45,667
Ah, sorry.

123
00:06:45,767 --> 00:06:48,133
You don't have to
answer if you don't want to.

124
00:06:48,233 --> 00:06:51,433
No, it's just... I did use him
as the model for my novel.

125
00:06:51,533 --> 00:06:53,300
Serizawa is definitely handsome.

126
00:06:54,767 --> 00:06:56,267
I see.

127
00:06:56,367 --> 00:06:57,367
Yeah.

128
00:06:57,433 --> 00:07:04,067
Besides, I've never...

129
00:07:04,167 --> 00:07:07,900
actually liked anyone before.

130
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,833
Not even once?

131
00:07:10,933 --> 00:07:13,467
You see, I get flustered easily.

132
00:07:13,567 --> 00:07:16,233
And when I'm nervous,
it shows all over my face.

133
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:20,767
Romance is just too hard for me.

134
00:07:20,867 --> 00:07:22,767
I really don't get it.

135
00:07:23,533 --> 00:07:27,433
You don't get it, huh...

136
00:07:29,167 --> 00:07:32,933
Then, for example...

137
00:07:33,033 --> 00:07:36,467
When you're hanging out with Serizawa...

138
00:07:37,567 --> 00:07:39,233
Does your heart ever race?

139
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:42,500
Heart... race...

140
00:07:48,033 --> 00:07:49,333
Good work.

141
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:51,433
Ah, sir.

142
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:54,633
I'm done writing.

143
00:07:54,733 --> 00:07:56,700
Oh, thanks.

144
00:08:01,133 --> 00:08:02,767
That's Takeuchi for you.

145
00:08:02,867 --> 00:08:04,600
You filled out the log very thoroughly.

146
00:08:04,967 --> 00:08:06,200
Thank you, sir.

147
00:08:08,233 --> 00:08:10,600
Thanks to you too, Suzuki, for helping out.

148
00:08:12,933 --> 00:08:14,100
Hmm?

149
00:08:14,733 --> 00:08:15,833
Suzuki?

150
00:08:15,933 --> 00:08:17,133
Hey.

151
00:08:20,933 --> 00:08:22,433
He completely froze.

152
00:08:28,067 --> 00:08:29,533
Heart... race...

153
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:38,600
That feeling just now... does
that count as my heart racing?

154
00:08:39,367 --> 00:08:41,133
It's a promise, then.

155
00:08:42,733 --> 00:08:45,867
Does that count as my heart racing too?

156
00:08:46,833 --> 00:08:47,833
Give it to me.

157
00:08:48,933 --> 00:08:50,267
Hey, wait.

158
00:08:50,367 --> 00:08:52,400
Come to think of it... do I?

159
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,600
- Huh?
- Ah, sorry.

160
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,167
Is my heart beating super fast right now?

161
00:08:58,267 --> 00:08:59,667
No, no.

162
00:09:01,233 --> 00:09:03,800
It'd be a lie to say my
heart hasn't raced at all.

163
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:07,133
But that's just because Serizawa
is my ideal seme.

164
00:09:07,233 --> 00:09:09,333
That's all it is.

165
00:09:19,633 --> 00:09:21,133
I really want to see him.

166
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:24,633
I said that's not it!

167
00:09:32,733 --> 00:09:34,300
I really want to see Suzuki.

168
00:09:44,633 --> 00:09:47,733
And now I'm actually here to see him.

169
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,633
(Serizawa)

170
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,433
But... Serizawa probably didn't expect...

171
00:09:54,533 --> 00:09:57,067
that I'd actually come to see him.

172
00:10:11,033 --> 00:10:13,433
I wonder if Serizawa is awake?

173
00:10:13,533 --> 00:10:17,500
I brought the class handouts
and bought some pudding for him.

174
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,567
I'll just leave them at your door.

175
00:10:19,667 --> 00:10:20,900
Get some good rest.

176
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,967
Suzuki.

177
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:31,133
Serizawa.

178
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:37,033
You actually came.

179
00:10:47,533 --> 00:10:49,500
Um... I...

180
00:10:49,867 --> 00:10:51,067
Come on in.

181
00:10:51,167 --> 00:10:52,700
No one else is home right now.

182
00:10:56,267 --> 00:10:57,700
Pardon the intrusion.

183
00:11:08,133 --> 00:11:09,600
This is my room.

184
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:12,833
So this is Serizawa's room.

185
00:11:12,933 --> 00:11:14,133
And...

186
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:17,233
These are all my collections.

187
00:11:19,433 --> 00:11:20,833
Ah!

188
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:22,567
They're all things I love.

189
00:11:26,233 --> 00:11:28,300
Serizawa's collection...?

190
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,867
Have a seat, Suzuki.

191
00:11:39,667 --> 00:11:40,933
Ah.

192
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:42,267
Okay.

193
00:11:47,833 --> 00:11:50,133
Serizawa's bed.

194
00:11:51,967 --> 00:11:54,400
Serizawa's loungewear.

195
00:11:56,133 --> 00:11:58,667
His sleeves are covering his
hands, and his hair is unstyled.

196
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,933
Oh no, he looks way too handsome.

197
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:06,233
What the heck am I thinking...?

198
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:11,100
Was my place easy to find?

199
00:12:12,967 --> 00:12:16,567
Yeah, Takeuchi walked me most of the way.

200
00:12:16,667 --> 00:12:18,100
Takeuchi?

201
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,300
Yeah.

202
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:25,533
Oh, right. You and Takeuchi went to
the same middle school, didn't you?

203
00:12:25,633 --> 00:12:28,167
I didn't know you guys lived
in the same neighborhood.

204
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:30,033
Yeah.

205
00:12:30,133 --> 00:12:31,333
We do.

206
00:12:31,433 --> 00:12:33,933
Did you guys come here together, though?

207
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:38,667
Yeah, I actually asked him
to come visit you with me.

208
00:12:38,767 --> 00:12:41,333
But he had something else going on.

209
00:12:41,433 --> 00:12:42,600
I see.

210
00:12:43,867 --> 00:12:45,367
What about lunch today?

211
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:46,733
Who did you eat with?

212
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,767
Same as always.

213
00:12:49,867 --> 00:12:51,567
I ate on the roof with the guys.

214
00:12:51,667 --> 00:12:52,909
What about the girls in our class?

215
00:12:52,933 --> 00:12:54,733
Did you talk to them at all?

216
00:12:54,833 --> 00:12:56,900
Oh, no, not really.

217
00:12:57,767 --> 00:12:59,233
Why?

218
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:01,533
Nothing.

219
00:13:02,367 --> 00:13:06,133
I was just a little worried.

220
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:07,600
Worried?

221
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:08,900
Yeah.

222
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:16,600
You know...

223
00:13:17,967 --> 00:13:21,367
I'm really glad you're getting
along with everyone, Suzuki.

224
00:13:22,033 --> 00:13:24,467
But don't get closer to
anyone else than you are to me.

225
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,933
- Wh-What did you say?
- Answer me.

226
00:13:31,967 --> 00:13:33,400
Do you understand?

227
00:13:34,067 --> 00:13:39,500
Y-Yeah, I got it.

228
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:43,833
I'm serious.

229
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:48,867
Wh-What is going on?

230
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:05,800
Suzuki.

231
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:10,100
Your ears are bright red.

232
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:17,033
Oh... Well...
I always turn red when I get nervous.

233
00:14:18,633 --> 00:14:20,067
Nervous?

234
00:14:20,667 --> 00:14:22,333
Are you nervous?

235
00:14:23,633 --> 00:14:26,400
Oh... no, it's just...

236
00:14:27,067 --> 00:14:30,533
So your heart races when you're with me?

237
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:36,500
I think...

238
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,967
Serizawa...

239
00:14:43,733 --> 00:14:45,033
Huh?

240
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:49,333
Wait, Serizawa, are you okay?

241
00:14:50,033 --> 00:14:52,600
- I'm totally fine...
- Are you sure?

242
00:14:54,067 --> 00:14:56,833
Wh-What should I do?

243
00:15:07,367 --> 00:15:08,833
Oh, you're awake.

244
00:15:11,067 --> 00:15:14,033
I fell asleep?

245
00:15:14,567 --> 00:15:16,033
How are you feeling?

246
00:15:16,933 --> 00:15:19,267
Here, have some water first.

247
00:15:20,233 --> 00:15:21,433
Thanks.

248
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,900
I feel a lot better now.

249
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,867
That's a relief.

250
00:15:41,967 --> 00:15:44,500
I thought you passed out.

251
00:15:45,667 --> 00:15:48,433
Oh, did you take your meds?

252
00:15:48,533 --> 00:15:49,933
Yeah.

253
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:51,267
Aren't you hungry?

254
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,767
I brought some jelly and pudding.

255
00:15:54,867 --> 00:15:56,067
Do you think you can eat?

256
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:03,000
I could if you fed me, Suzuki.

257
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:05,533
You can feed yourself just fine.

258
00:16:05,633 --> 00:16:06,833
Come on, what's the big deal?

259
00:16:06,933 --> 00:16:08,333
Just this once.

260
00:16:09,067 --> 00:16:12,867
Besides, a vulnerable seme
has its own charm, right?

261
00:16:14,133 --> 00:16:16,600
I guess so.

262
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,600
Mhm.

263
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:21,633
A-Alright, fine.

264
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,700
Here.

265
00:16:44,167 --> 00:16:45,600
How is it?

266
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:50,300
Amazing.

267
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:53,200
So comforting.

268
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,133
Hm?

269
00:16:57,233 --> 00:16:58,467
What's wrong?

270
00:16:58,533 --> 00:16:59,700
Nothing.

271
00:17:01,033 --> 00:17:05,333
I was just thinking that you
really are like the sun, Serizawa.

272
00:17:06,367 --> 00:17:07,600
The sun?

273
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:08,967
Yeah.

274
00:17:09,367 --> 00:17:10,633
It wasn't until...

275
00:17:11,833 --> 00:17:12,967
our second year

276
00:17:13,067 --> 00:17:16,567
that we ended up in the same class, right?

277
00:17:17,167 --> 00:17:17,767
Serizawa!

278
00:17:17,867 --> 00:17:19,307
- Hey!
- We're all in the same class!

279
00:17:19,367 --> 00:17:20,733
- Same class!
- Yeah!

280
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:21,833
Yeah!

281
00:17:21,933 --> 00:17:23,100
Woo!

282
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,767
Here I come!

283
00:17:24,867 --> 00:17:26,309
What kind of chicken scratch is this?

284
00:17:26,333 --> 00:17:27,667
Are you sure about this?

285
00:17:27,767 --> 00:17:29,667
I might need to double-check that...

286
00:17:29,967 --> 00:17:32,200
You were already pretty popular.

287
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:34,333
I'd definitely heard your name around.

288
00:17:34,433 --> 00:17:38,233
But at first, I didn't really know
what kind of guy you were.

289
00:17:40,233 --> 00:17:41,600
But...

290
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,267
Suzuki, you dropped this.

291
00:17:51,767 --> 00:17:53,100
Here.

292
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:56,900
Th-Thanks.

293
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:01,200
It wasn't until we shared a
class that I finally realized.

294
00:18:03,033 --> 00:18:04,300
- Iwasaki.
- Hm?

295
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,433
Suzuki.

296
00:18:05,533 --> 00:18:07,400
- Shut up!
- We're all going to hang out.

297
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,433
Wanna come with us?

298
00:18:12,267 --> 00:18:13,867
Sorry...

299
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:15,967
I'm not really good
with that kind of stuff.

300
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:17,700
Gotcha.

301
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:19,567
My bad for springing it on you.

302
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:26,600
You treat everyone the same.
You're so kind and upbeat.

303
00:18:29,033 --> 00:18:31,367
Whenever I see you smile,

304
00:18:31,467 --> 00:18:33,633
it just brightens my day.

305
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,467
Back then, just the thought of
going to school depressed me.

306
00:18:43,367 --> 00:18:47,333
To me, you really are
like the sun, Serizawa.

307
00:18:52,400 --> 00:19:00,400
So with you gone today,
the classroom felt really empty.

308
00:19:05,933 --> 00:19:08,033
Why are you suddenly saying all this?

309
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,133
It makes me so happy.

310
00:19:15,567 --> 00:19:17,500
Anyway,

311
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,633
I had no idea you thought of me like that.

312
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,700
Oh... Oh, right.

313
00:19:25,967 --> 00:19:29,000
Your fever should be down by now, right?

314
00:19:36,667 --> 00:19:40,533
My hands are too cold to tell.

315
00:19:42,567 --> 00:19:44,167
Huh?

316
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:46,500
Hold still a sec, Serizawa.

317
00:19:46,867 --> 00:19:47,867
Okay.

318
00:19:58,267 --> 00:20:01,633
Looks like your fever broke.

319
00:20:04,867 --> 00:20:05,933
Oh...

320
00:20:06,033 --> 00:20:07,667
I-I'm sorry.

321
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:13,233
No... thanks, Suzuki.

322
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,500
I feel completely fine now.

323
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:19,500
Oh, good.

324
00:20:20,867 --> 00:20:22,400
That's a relief.

325
00:20:24,133 --> 00:20:27,000
But you still need to stay in bed and rest.

326
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:30,800
I should probably get going anyway.

327
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,433
Don't.

328
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:39,167
Don't go.

329
00:20:40,933 --> 00:20:46,667
But your family should be
getting back soon, right?

330
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:50,333
It's fine. No one's home today.

331
00:20:50,567 --> 00:20:51,400
Huh?

332
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:54,700
My mom's working the night
shift, and my dad's out of town.

333
00:20:55,333 --> 00:20:58,933
My brother's on a trip with his friends.

334
00:20:59,933 --> 00:21:04,367
So stay with me a little longer, Suzuki.

335
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,533
I'll get lonely.

336
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,300
Sleep next to me.

337
00:21:17,367 --> 00:21:19,400
(Serizawa)

338
00:21:24,633 --> 00:21:27,367
Wh-What is going on?

339
00:21:27,467 --> 00:21:30,833
Um, Serizawa, I...

340
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:35,233
Suzuki, I don't want you
to look at me. Turn around.

341
00:21:36,133 --> 00:21:37,200
Oh.

342
00:21:38,433 --> 00:21:39,700
Why?

343
00:21:40,067 --> 00:21:41,567
W-Wait a sec.

344
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:49,500
It's easier for me to
fall asleep like this.

345
00:21:50,067 --> 00:21:52,233
You're being so selfish.

346
00:21:54,433 --> 00:21:58,533
Don't tell me... your heart is racing?

347
00:21:58,967 --> 00:22:00,400
N-No, it's not.

348
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,433
You're so cute.

349
00:22:04,867 --> 00:22:06,900
Stop messing with me, Serizawa.

350
00:22:09,533 --> 00:22:11,600
What should I do?

351
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:14,133
This is bad. What is going on?

352
00:22:16,033 --> 00:22:18,233
I... I should probably head home.

353
00:22:18,767 --> 00:22:20,267
No.

354
00:22:20,367 --> 00:22:21,733
Don't go.

355
00:22:22,833 --> 00:22:24,600
Stay with me until morning.

356
00:22:26,433 --> 00:22:28,800
St-Stay until morning?

357
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:31,967
Crap.

358
00:22:32,467 --> 00:22:34,033
What is happening?

359
00:22:44,233 --> 00:22:50,333
Could I actually...

360
00:22:51,467 --> 00:22:58,133
be falling for Serizawa?

361
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,800
(Next Episode)

362
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:14,667
(This drama is a work of fiction)
Suzuki, you actually like me, don't you?
